generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    - Design a "cavity template" — an LR-symmetric layout of 4-9 cavity slots, each with
      (row_rank, col_rank, center_position, seed_bbox). Layout defines POSITIONS only;
      shapes come from the next steps. Pack slots tightly (allow diagonal-adjacent slots).
    - Build the output grid (filled dst) by mutating each template slot's shape independently
      — start from the seed bbox and randomly add/remove boundary cells while keeping the
      cavity 4-connected. Aim for ~50% non-rectangular mutations (L, T, cross, staircase,
      notched rectangles, organic blobs). Neighboring cavities are ALLOWED to touch
      diagonally (4-disconnected, 8-connected). Assign a fill color to each cavity. Wrap
      the entire fill mask in a 1-cell outline (outline cells are the bg neighbors of any
      fill cell under 4-connectivity). LR-symmetry is maintained by mutating mirror-pair
      slots with mirrored operations.
    - Derive dst from output by replacing all fill pixels with bg. The result is a single
      8-connected outline-only object with empty holes in the same positions as src's
      cavities.
    - Independently build src from the same cavity template by mutating each slot's shape
      AGAIN with a FRESH random seed — src subsprite shapes MUST visibly differ from dst
      hole shapes. Wrap with outline and fill
      each cavity with the assigned color. src is 1 connected component. Do NOT reuse the
      dst shape array for src — always run the mutation independently.
    - Place src and dst on a 22-30 x 22-30 bg canvas. They may overlap spatially as long
      as pixels don't collide. Verify main(input) == expected output.
